   "source": [
    "# Reaction Video Editor — Colab Version\n",
    "\n",
    "**What this is:** A Python pipeline combining both repo variants (root original + `diffrent variant`) for processing reaction videos inside Google Colab.\n",
    "\n",
    "**What it does:**\n",
    "- Splits 3840×1080 OBS side-by-side recordings into camera / content halves.\n",
    "- Composes reaction layout (camera top-left rounded, content bottom-right rounded, blurred background 50%/op 40%).\n",
    "- Mixes 2-track audio with compressor / limiter / sidechain ducking.\n",
    "- Auto-cuts silent/repeated reaction segments for seamless flow.\n",
    "- Transcribes intro/outro via Whisper to fix pauses/repeats.\n",
    "- Applies face retouch (smooth, teeth, nose, eyes) with MediaPipe tracking.\n",
    "- Exports MP4 and WebM to Google Drive.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Where computing happens:** Inside this Colab VM (CPU; GPU if you enable GPU runtime). Large 3 GB files stream through `ffmpeg`, they are not loaded fully into RAM.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Will WebM upload to YouTube?** Yes — YouTube fully accepts VP9/WebM. We export both MP4 (H.264) and WebM (VP9/Opus) so you can pick either.\n",
    "\n",
    "**How to preserve output:** We write to `/content/drive/MyDrive/...` immediately, so files survive session termination (Colab deletes `/tmp` when session dies)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# 1) Install dependencies (run once per session)")
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "!pip install -q numpy opencv-python mediapipe openai-whisper ffmpeg-python moviepy pydub"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2) Mount Google Drive"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from google.colab import drive\n",
    "drive.mount('/content/drive')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3) Import processor and configure paths"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import sys, os\n",
    "sys.path.insert(0, '/content/VideoEditorTool/colab_version')  # adjust if repo cloned elsewhere\n",
    "from video_processor import ReactionVideoProcessor\n",
    "\n",
    "# Point to your raw OBS recording (3840x1080 side-by-side)\n",
    "input_video = '/content/drive/MyDrive/raw/recording_3840.mp4'   # <-- change this\n",
    "output_dir = '/content/drive/MyDrive/reaction_output'         # <-- and this\n",
    "\n",
    "proc = ReactionVideoProcessor(input_video, output_dir=output_dir)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4) Patreon version — full uncut + intro/outro cleaned\n",
    "\n",
    "- Intro / outro kept in full camera (safe, no copyrighted content).\n",
    "- Reaction part composed with layout preset.\n",
    "- Whispers intro to detect pauses / repeats for manual edit.\n",
    "- Audio mixed with compression and ducking."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "proc.run_patron_version(\n",
    "    intro_range=(12, 55),      # seconds — intro section to clean/transcribe\n",
    "    outro_range=(1260, 1300),  # seconds — outro section\n",
    "    preset='diagonal',         # camera top-left / content bottom-right\n",
    "    retouch=False,             # set True if you want skin smooth + eye/nose/teeth\n",
    "    fix_intro=True            # runs Whisper and saves intro_transcript.json\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5) YouTube version — reaction with alterations + auto-cuts\n",
    "\n",
    "- Middle reaction gets auto-cut silence / repeated parts (`auto_cut=True`).\n",
    "- Camera half is retouched (`retouch=True`) — tracking rebuilds mask every frame.\n",
    "- Custom cuts can be passed as `custom_cuts=[(t1,t2), ...]` if you already know bad spots.\n",
    "- Layout preset `diagonal` gives the corrected layout you asked for."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "proc.run_youtube_version(\n",
    "    preset='diagonal',\n",
    "    auto_cut=True,\n",
    "    retouch=True,\n",
    "    intro_range=(12, 55),\n",
    "    outro_range=(1260, 1300),\n",
    "    # custom_cuts=[(340, 375), (892, 905)]  # uncomment if you know bad segments\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
